From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mcla-x86 SDK patch layer
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0600: swap_post_effect live (FXAA switches while playing); texture_lod_bias (sampler mip bias, live)

Source: Ours, written for this SDK (VISUALS stream). Tested in runs vis1/vis2/vis3-parked-ab ($WORK/runs): the
  `swap_post_effect: <name> (live)` line follows each change on the next swap; FXAA visibly smooths edges
  (scratch/VIS/audit/vis2_edge.png); cost about +0.3 ms GPU at 1080p on a Radeon 880M (pooled A/B, noise +-0.3 ms).
Licence: GPL-3 (owner's own work, part of mcla-x86); the patched files are ReXGlue SDK code (BSD-3-Clause)
Purpose: (1) swap_post_effect (none, fxaa, fxaa_extreme) was applied once at graphics start. The command processor now
  re-reads the cvar string on every swap (one short string compare when unchanged) and switches the effect on the CP thread
  (D3D12 and Vulkan), so a launcher, a preset applied after graphics start, an in-game A/B schedule or a frame-rate
  governor can change it while playing. HDR output is unchanged: while the HDR10 swap chain is active the existing code
  forces no FXAA, and the cvar's value comes back when HDR is off. The parser moved to CommandProcessor::ParseSwapPostEffect.
  (2) texture_lod_bias (default 0 = as shipped, range [-1.875, 0]): added to the sampler MipLODBias of every mipmapped,
  non-base-map texture, in the existing 4-bit 1/8-level lod_bias field of the sampler key (so a change makes new samplers:
  live), on top of the TAA/FSR squeeze bias. The guest's own per-fetch bias in the shaders is untouched.
Bucket: REDO (new, written for this port)
